WEBVTT

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:04.420
"Dear Hase-sama...

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:08.690
I've finished unpacking my things, 
and everything is going fine.

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.870
Three years ago, I lost my parents

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:18.710
and had to live with relatives.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:22.740
But now, I've finally taken my first 
step toward real independence.

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:27.450
But there's one problem, I guess...

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:32.340
In this yokai apartment building,

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:35.040
humans and monsters live together."

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:38.070
No, no!

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:41.130
If I write this, he'll think I'm crazy!

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:43.820
What's bugging you, chirp, Yushi?

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:47.050
Hey, worry too much, 
and you'll go bald, chirp.

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:48.980
Be careful, chirp!

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:51.810
My independent life...

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:53.020
Chirpity-chirp!

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:29.160
<b>Second Haunting 
The Residents of the Yokai Apartments</b>

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:32.020
What's wrong, Yushi-kun?

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:35.530
Are you not enjoying the meal Ruriruri made?

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:44.640
<b>Reimei Isshiki</b>

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.380
<i>Reimei Isshiki.</i>

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:41.750
<i>A poet of unknown age.</i>

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:43.430
<i>He's human.</i>

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:44.640
<b>Human</b>

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:46.490
You need to eat, Yushi-kun...

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:48.620
School starts soon, doesn't it?

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:51.050
You need to eat and build your stamina.

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:58.490
<b>Akine Kuga</b>

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:55.070
<i>Akine Kuga-san. Also human.</i>

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:57.370
<i>She's an exorcist... supposedly.</i>

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:58.490
<b>Human</b>

00:02:58.480 --> 00:02:59.750
Morning!

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:02.190
Wow, this smells good!

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:05.060
Sato-san and Yamada-san, good morning.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.550
<i>And they're ghosts.</i>

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:13.000
<b>Ghosts</b>

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:10.460
<i>No... Spirits? Yokai?</i>

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:13.000
<b>Spirits</b>

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:10.620
<b>Yokai</b>

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:11.210
<b>Ghost</b>

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:12.390
<i>Jeez, I don't even know!</i>

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:12.750
<b>Yokai</b>

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:13.000
<b>Yokai</b>

00:03:12.990 --> 00:03:16.780
I'm going on a training trip for my new job.

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:18.690
I'll be in Hakone for a week.

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:20.230
Nice, Sato-san.

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:22.220
That's Soir Cosmetics for you.

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:23.800
They're willing to spend big.

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:25.360
<i>He's got a job?</i>

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:26.630
<i>And with a big company?!</i>

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:40.310
<i>I can touch them.</i>

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:44.110
<i>S-So cute...</i>

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:48.410
<i>But aren't they ghosts, too?</i>

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:50.890
Wondering why you can touch ghosts?

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:55.810
This building's grounds are within 
a special barrier that stabilizes

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:57.920
the souls of the dead.

00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:02.800
That's why you can see and touch 
things that you normally can't.

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:05.330
There's also a path to another dimension.

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:09.040
And in some places, several dimensions 
overlap or are out of phase,

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:09.920
and then...

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:12.390
I... I don't understand any of that.

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:18.510
So, decide what you're going to do?

00:04:19.710 --> 00:04:22.470
Will you stay here until 
your dorm is repaired?

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:24.540
Or go back and live with your uncle?

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:31.410
Yeah, I guess he will.

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:39.530
I'm staying here. It's only six months.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:40.970
I see.

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:43.630
That's great! Just what I wanted to hear!

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:47.040
Look! Ruriko-san made you a cake!

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:48.650
Huh? For me?

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:50.190
Looks delicious!

00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:53.730
Everything Ruriruri makes is delicious!

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:55.170
Right?

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:58.810
Yushi-kun, you don't care if 
Ruriko-san is a ghost, right?

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:00.210
Of course not!

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:03.110
No matter what kind of ghost 
she is, I wouldn't care!

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:06.190
Hear that? Isn't that nice, Ruriruri?

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:18.750
<b>Joutou Business High School</b>

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:18.750
<i>And so, my high school life began.</i>

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:21.410
I just saw someone who looked really cool!

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:23.580
Hey, let's exchange our email addresses!

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:26.000
So yesterday, my dad said...

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:27.920
<i>That's right...</i>

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:30.630
<i>People call stuff like this normal.</i>

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:32.770
<i>But at my place...</i>

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:35.910
Why do you look so bored?

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:40.310
It's your first day at a 
new school! Cheer up!

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:43.400
I'm Takenaka, by the way. What's up?

00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:46.750
R-Right... Hello.

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:02.950
Just six more months!

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:07.350
Welcome back.

00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:08.430
I'm back.

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:09.300
Wait.

00:06:15.970 --> 00:06:18.480
Oh, that's Hanako-san.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:20.010
Hanako-san?

00:06:20.010 --> 00:06:21.760
She's always in the front hall.

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:24.910
And she says "goodbye" and "welcome back."

00:06:24.910 --> 00:06:26.240
Is that all?

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:28.240
Yep. That's all.

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:32.530
Don't worry, you'll eventually 
be able to see her, too.

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:35.480
I will?! And you aren't scared?

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:37.590
Ghosts and yokai are everywhere!

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:38.910
Scared?

00:06:39.820 --> 00:06:41.950
We're all friends, and they're fun.

00:06:41.950 --> 00:06:43.050
Friends?

00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:45.170
They are like we are.

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:47.860
In their own way, they are 
trying to live normal lives.

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:50.640
Some of them are good and some are bad.

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:53.390
It's just like us.

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:57.300
Just like us... I don't know.

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:03.180
W-Wolf ghost!

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:04.360
Idiot.

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:06.640
You're a man. Don't scare so easily.

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:09.520
Welcome back, Akira-san! Cigar!

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:12.660
Been a long time since we 
had a new human resident.

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:15.280
Doesn't he look glum?

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:18.150
This is the new guy, Yushi Inaba-kun.

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:21.390
I'm Akira Fukase, in room 103.

00:07:21.390 --> 00:07:22.790
I'm a painter.

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:24.200
This is Cigar.

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:25.240
A painter?

00:07:25.240 --> 00:07:28.690
Yeah, he's an old friend of mine.

00:07:29.290 --> 00:07:32.300
Does that mean you're human, Fukase-san?

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:33.760
Listen up, kid!

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:38.420
Here, it doesn't mean a damn thing 
whether you're human or not.

00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:40.120
I've lived here ten years,

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:42.070
without any problems whatsoever.

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:42.930
Got it?

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:44.480
Y-Yeah...

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:47.160
Hello there, young man. Having some trouble?

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:50.900
Seems you're having trouble 
in your relationships.

00:07:51.230 --> 00:07:53.790
U-Um...

00:07:54.630 --> 00:07:55.520
Who are you?

00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:58.700
Today, I will introduce you 
to something great!

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:00.240
Look at this.

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:04.740
A unicorn horn, to drive off wicked 
thoughts and purify your body.

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:08.850
Carry this with you, and your 
problems will instantly vanish.

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:13.370
Act now, and I'll give you a discount.

00:08:13.750 --> 00:08:15.310
No way! No way! No way! No way!

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:18.880
Stay away from the new kid.

00:08:18.880 --> 00:08:22.090
Sorry, Yushi-kun... That must've scared you.

00:08:22.090 --> 00:08:25.070
You haven't changed, Antiquary.

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:27.300
Antiquary-san?

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:28.450
Correct.

00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:31.560
If you're after something, 
talk to me whenever you like.

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:38.040
Who are those people with him?

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:39.910
I think he calls them "automata."

00:08:39.910 --> 00:08:43.290
Huh? I heard they were homunculi.

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:47.990
While in foreign lands,

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:50.460
how many times did I dream 
of this delicious food?

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:51.870
Damn right...

00:08:51.870 --> 00:08:53.250
Thank you, Ruriko!

00:08:57.690 --> 00:08:59.140
That bath was so nice!

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:09.440
This is the only way to end a bath!

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:11.150
I feel so refreshed!

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:15.270
Stop walking around like that, Mariko-chan.

00:09:15.270 --> 00:09:16.480
Oh, my.

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:18.220
You look beautiful again today.

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:21.420
You're so honest, Antiquary-san.

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:23.290
Careful, new kid...

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:26.200
She might not look it, 
but she's incredibly old.

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:28.590
Shaddup! Who you callin' old?!

00:09:29.270 --> 00:09:30.370
Oh?

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:35.330
You're so cute! You're new, aren't you?

00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:36.170
What's your name?

00:09:36.170 --> 00:09:38.140
Y-Yushi Inaba!

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:40.790
I'm Mariko. Nice to meet you.

00:09:40.790 --> 00:09:43.240
I have my reasons for not going to heaven.

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:44.630
You're a ghost?!

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:48.800
How about I teach you a few things?

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:52.990
Mariko-san, don't tease him too much.

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:56.070
S-Stop it, please!

00:10:02.150 --> 00:10:04.580
Was that too much?

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:07.740
No, don't worry, Yushi-kun.

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:11.330
That's right.

00:10:11.330 --> 00:10:13.500
He's back.

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:21.890
The psychic in room 203, Ryu-san.

00:10:22.590 --> 00:10:24.320
He's probably... human.

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:26.980
Ryu-san?

00:10:28.930 --> 00:10:31.950
<i>Wow! All the yokai are bowing!</i>

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:34.600
<i>Is he really...</i>

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:36.640
Ryu-san, it's been a while.

00:10:36.640 --> 00:10:38.360
Welcome back, Ryu-san!

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:39.240
Yo.

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:43.870
Isshiki-san, hello there.

00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:46.380
Is this a new resident? That's rare.

00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:50.150
Yushi Inaba-kun. A first-year JTB student.

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:53.220
His dorm burned down, so he's 
here for six months.

00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:55.480
I see. Sorry to hear that.

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:58.310
Th-Thank you! Nice to meet you!

00:10:58.310 --> 00:11:01.270
Nice to meet you. 
Everyone calls me "Ryu-san."

00:11:01.270 --> 00:11:03.170
I'm a down-on-my-luck psychic.

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:05.050
Psychic?

00:11:06.990 --> 00:11:09.280
Is there something you wish to ask?

00:11:12.700 --> 00:11:17.830
Why are there so many yokai 
in this apartment building?

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:23.360
For them, this is an oasis in the desert.

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:25.110
Oasis?

00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:28.410
Grass, soil, and water were 
once more abundant,

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:30.650
and human hearts were also more full.

00:11:30.650 --> 00:11:32.350
There was much darkness,

00:11:32.350 --> 00:11:35.120
and the world's mysteries were 
always by our side.

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:39.270
But now, all that is lost,

00:11:39.270 --> 00:11:42.030
and humanity has closed its heart.

00:11:43.290 --> 00:11:46.540
While humanity pursued convenience,

00:11:46.540 --> 00:11:49.130
the mysteries lost their place to belong.

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:52.310
Is... that right?

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:55.060
But whether that's good or bad,

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:57.080
I doubt you will find an answer.

00:11:57.420 --> 00:11:59.150
Because over time,

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:01.780
nothing ever stays exactly the same.

00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:06.200
The lives humans live, the world 
of nature, and the yokai...

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:08.490
They constantly change.

00:12:09.170 --> 00:12:10.880
Constantly change?

00:12:11.330 --> 00:12:15.000
I think this apartment building 
will be good for you.

00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:20.050
Pain and sadness are only one 
part of a much larger world.

00:12:21.290 --> 00:12:23.890
As long as you are willing to allow it,

00:12:23.890 --> 00:12:26.140
more will seem normal to you.

00:12:26.540 --> 00:12:27.850
For example,

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:32.020
by coming here, being able to see 
ghosts has become normal.

00:12:32.930 --> 00:12:37.100
Your life is long, and the world 
stretches out, without end.

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:44.960
So relax.

00:12:59.890 --> 00:13:03.220
Huh? "Akine Kuga" isn't your real name?

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:07.650
That's right. We psychics hide our names.

00:13:07.650 --> 00:13:11.440
My technique is "Kuga-style Shinnenjutsu."

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:14.140
It's all about training the mind.

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:17.430
In sixth grade, I was given permission 
to use the Kuga name.

00:13:17.430 --> 00:13:20.430
And now, I'm an apprentice 
at Tsukinoki Hospital.

00:13:20.430 --> 00:13:22.680
Then, the hospital is...

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:24.850
Naturally, it's a yokai hospital.

00:13:24.850 --> 00:13:27.440
It looks like a normal hospital, though.

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:33.160
Okay, good luck with your studies!

00:13:35.900 --> 00:13:38.750
A psychic and a yokai hospital, huh?

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:40.610
That's kind of amazing.

00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:42.870
It's a whole different world from mine.

00:13:47.770 --> 00:13:50.720
Inaba, on our way home, 
let's hang out somewhere.

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:52.680
I know a good place.

00:13:53.590 --> 00:13:55.500
No, I...

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:58.420
Too bad. Inaba-kun's busy.

00:13:58.420 --> 00:14:00.510
Let's head to club, Inaba-kun.

00:14:01.010 --> 00:14:04.230
This is Tashiro. She's in the English 
Conversation Club with me.

00:14:04.600 --> 00:14:08.770
Hey, why did you decide to join 
the English Conversation Club?

00:14:08.770 --> 00:14:10.230
Why?

00:14:10.230 --> 00:14:11.930
I don't mind learning English.

00:14:11.930 --> 00:14:14.310
I thought it would help 
when I look for a job.

00:14:14.310 --> 00:14:16.490
Wow, you actually put some thought into it!

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:20.580
I just figured that if I could 
speak English, it'd be cool!

00:14:20.580 --> 00:14:21.390
I mean,

00:14:21.390 --> 00:14:24.420
wouldn't it be awesome to watch 
movies in English without subtitles?

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:28.050
<i>I was surprised by something in high school.</i>

00:14:28.540 --> 00:14:30.640
<i>Girls started talking to me normally,</i>

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:33.160
<i>like Akine-chan and Tashiro.</i>

00:14:33.960 --> 00:14:35.970
<i>The only girl I had any experience with...</i>

00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:40.920
<i>If I even came near her, she got mad.</i>

00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:44.030
<i>Come to think of it, didn't Hase 
once say something about that?</i>

00:14:44.030 --> 00:14:48.140
It's because of your aura. It says, 
"If you get close, I'll kill you."

00:14:48.660 --> 00:14:50.530
<i>Maybe he was right.</i>

00:14:51.400 --> 00:14:54.150
<i>My parents died, and my whole life changed.</i>

00:14:54.150 --> 00:14:57.210
<i>And I was so scared by what 
was happening to me...</i>

00:14:57.790 --> 00:15:00.960
<i>I lost the ability to really smile.</i>

00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:01.950
<i>But...</i>

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:05.380
<b>English Conversation Club 
Cross-Cultural Communication Party 
*Barbecue</b>

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:05.370
Okay, let's hear some ideas from 
the new students, too!

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:05.380
<b>Club President</b>

00:15:05.710 --> 00:15:07.460
I want to put on a play.

00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:09.130
A musical would also be nice.

00:15:09.430 --> 00:15:12.760
<i>Am I starting to change a little?</i>

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:15.410
You think, as well, Inaba-kun!

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:20.080
Bye-bye. See you around.

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:21.010
Yeah.

00:15:27.110 --> 00:15:29.550
I wonder if they're stopping somewhere, too.

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:42.960
<i>Wh-What is this?</i>

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:44.860
<i>What happened to Tashiro?</i>

00:15:48.170 --> 00:15:49.210
<i>No...</i>

00:15:49.730 --> 00:15:51.830
<i>I've got a really bad feeling.</i>

00:15:56.180 --> 00:15:57.440
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:15:57.730 --> 00:15:59.360
<i>Bad, bad, bad!</i>

00:16:00.870 --> 00:16:01.840
Tashiro!

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:16.100
T-Ta-ko... Ta-ko!

00:16:17.920 --> 00:16:18.910
Tashiro!

00:16:19.200 --> 00:16:20.290
It hurts...

00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:22.710
Hang in there! I'll call an ambulance!

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:24.090
It hurts so much!

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:27.110
Help me,

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:29.690
Inaba-kun.

00:16:34.770 --> 00:16:36.850
I knew this would happen.

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:41.000
I knew you were in danger, and I...

00:16:57.400 --> 00:16:58.690
What is this?

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:00.030
Yushi-kun!

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:01.580
Akine-san—

00:17:03.880 --> 00:17:07.410
Huh? What happened to me?

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:12.210
It's okay, Yushi-kun.

00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:15.290
She's already stopped bleeding.

00:17:15.290 --> 00:17:16.870
You stopped it.

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:20.760
Hold on. I'll get it out of you now.

00:17:27.550 --> 00:17:28.700
What happened?

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:30.570
I feel so much better.

00:17:33.510 --> 00:17:34.700
Good work!

00:17:36.300 --> 00:17:37.420
Thanks.

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:44.910
Chirp... Chirpity-chirp. Chirp...

00:17:45.260 --> 00:17:46.250
Gimme more!

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:47.780
Sure, sure.

00:17:47.780 --> 00:17:49.490
Your reward for good work!

00:17:49.490 --> 00:17:51.630
But I couldn't do anything for Tashiro.

00:17:51.990 --> 00:17:55.050
Nope, you saved her!

00:17:56.640 --> 00:17:57.610
I did?

00:17:57.960 --> 00:18:02.070
You said that when you saw her, 
you felt really tired, right?

00:18:02.070 --> 00:18:06.490
That was because you took on 
the burden of her injuries.

00:18:06.790 --> 00:18:09.760
I took on... her injuries?

00:18:11.350 --> 00:18:15.080
This is the ability to synchronize 
with another person.

00:18:15.080 --> 00:18:18.280
Psychic healing often uses this method.

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:22.600
First, you transfer the damage 
to a stronger body...

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:26.870
When the damage is gone, you heal the injury.

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:30.460
Then, I take the damage that you took.

00:18:33.060 --> 00:18:34.200
And let it escape!

00:18:35.780 --> 00:18:39.750
This time, all of the coincidences 
made your antennae perk up.

00:18:39.750 --> 00:18:40.740
Don't worry.

00:18:40.740 --> 00:18:42.890
Yep, that's what happened!

00:18:42.890 --> 00:18:45.130
Y-Yeah.

00:18:45.130 --> 00:18:49.780
I don't really care, but don't make 
me worry too much, new kid.

00:18:50.430 --> 00:18:52.190
You were worried?

00:18:52.190 --> 00:18:53.650
Of course.

00:18:53.650 --> 00:18:56.480
Everyone here is friends.

00:18:56.490 --> 00:18:57.780
Friends...

00:18:59.410 --> 00:19:01.320
<b>Takanodai Central Hospital</b>

00:18:59.410 --> 00:19:01.890
Hey, listen to this!

00:19:01.890 --> 00:19:04.790
They said I nicked an artery in my leg.

00:19:04.790 --> 00:19:07.860
But when I got to the hospital, 
the bleeding had stopped.

00:19:07.860 --> 00:19:10.030
The doctors were really surprised!

00:19:10.030 --> 00:19:12.290
You were lucky, huh?

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:13.440
Right?

00:19:13.440 --> 00:19:15.490
I'm glad you were there, Inaba-kun.

00:19:15.490 --> 00:19:16.670
You really saved me!

00:19:17.750 --> 00:19:19.630
I didn't do anything.

00:19:19.630 --> 00:19:20.850
No...

00:19:21.340 --> 00:19:25.420
When it happened, it hurt 
so much, I thought I'd die.

00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:28.280
But when I saw your face,

00:19:28.280 --> 00:19:31.150
I suddenly started to feel better.

00:19:32.290 --> 00:19:36.250
It was like you sucked away all of my pain!

00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:37.300
Really.

00:19:38.450 --> 00:19:42.280
<i>Then, Tashiro felt the synchronization, too.</i>

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:45.500
I don't know why,

00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:47.460
but I really did feel like that.

00:19:47.920 --> 00:19:50.430
It was so strange.

00:19:50.770 --> 00:19:52.610
Y-Yeah...

00:19:57.840 --> 00:19:58.880
Thank you!

00:20:16.350 --> 00:20:18.910
<i>"I discovered a power I didn't know I had.</i>

00:20:19.640 --> 00:20:21.210
<i>And not only that.</i>

00:20:21.210 --> 00:20:23.860
<i>What's inside my heart, as well."</i>

00:20:24.210 --> 00:20:28.410
Your life is long, and the world 
stretches out, without end.

00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:30.870
So relax.

00:20:34.060 --> 00:20:37.130
<i>"Yeah, I'm having a lot of fun.</i>

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:39.270
<i>Come and hang out, sometime."</i>

00:20:40.790 --> 00:20:42.710
The rest of this is homework, okay?

00:20:42.710 --> 00:20:45.540
It's the start of a new year, 
so don't forget.

00:20:45.540 --> 00:20:47.800
<i>I still can't tell him about this...</i>

00:20:47.800 --> 00:20:50.020
<i>He'll think I'm crazy.</i>

00:20:50.020 --> 00:20:51.400
Hey, Inaba!

00:20:51.400 --> 00:20:53.030
Going to the cafeteria, too?

00:20:53.030 --> 00:20:54.440
Want to come with us?

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:55.890
S-Sure!

00:20:55.890 --> 00:20:58.230
Where's my wallet?

00:20:59.600 --> 00:21:01.490
What? You've got a lunch.

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:03.780
You guys who room somewhere are lucky!

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:12.790
<b>Hang in there, Yushi-kun! 
— Ruriko</b>

00:21:13.400 --> 00:21:14.650
Ruriko-san...

00:21:14.990 --> 00:21:16.120
Yushi-kun!

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:21.920
<b>Hang in there, Yushi-kun! 
— Ruriko</b>

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:17.660
Hey, new kid!

00:21:31.810 --> 00:21:33.300
This is great!

00:21:33.300 --> 00:21:35.610
Ruriko-san's the best!

00:23:10.350 --> 00:23:13.910
Akine-san, is that kid, Kuri, really a ghost?

00:23:13.910 --> 00:23:14.940
That's right.

00:23:14.940 --> 00:23:18.150
So sometimes, he'll show up 
in other people's photos

00:23:18.150 --> 00:23:20.150
or appear in your bed,

00:23:20.150 --> 00:23:23.160
screaming, "You will suffer!"

00:23:23.160 --> 00:23:25.000
Be careful, Yushi-kun!

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:26.460
No, that's definitely a lie.

00:23:27.670 --> 00:23:30.830
Next time on <i>Elegant Yokai Apartment Life</i>:

00:23:30.430 --> 00:23:32.470
<b>Third Haunting 
Kuri and Shiro</b>

00:23:30.830 --> 00:23:31.980
Kuri and Shiro.

00:23:32.470 --> 00:23:35.050
What is a mother, anyway?
